1
00:00:25,791 --> 00:00:28,881
Well then, what can I do?

2
00:00:30,301 --> 00:00:33,471
How can I protect my country from these fools?

3
00:00:37,301 --> 00:00:40,141
As a reward for saving the prince,

4
00:00:40,221 --> 00:00:43,021
the king presents you with 50 pounds of silver.

5
00:00:43,101 --> 00:00:44,941
Accept it with gratitude.

6
00:00:46,601 --> 00:00:51,401
I heard that you fought hard to save Canute.

7
00:00:51,481 --> 00:00:53,111
Accept my gratitude.

8
00:00:53,941 --> 00:00:56,781
Yes, Your Highness. Thank you for your reward.

9
00:00:59,451 --> 00:01:04,751
I have high expectations of you
in our battle to subjugate Wales.

10
00:01:07,711 --> 00:01:11,631
It appears that sly old fox has noticed.

11
00:01:14,131 --> 00:01:17,761
Your Highness, with all due respect,

12
00:01:22,811 --> 00:01:25,311
are you sure that your plan to subjugate Wales

13
00:01:27,601 --> 00:01:31,191
is the best decision?

14
00:03:05,081 --> 00:03:06,741
END OF THE PROLOGUE

15
00:03:06,831 --> 00:03:11,041
I believe the campaign to subjugate Wales next spring
will prove to be a fruitless battle for our army.

16
00:03:12,501 --> 00:03:14,461
Please, reconsider the matter.

17
00:03:15,461 --> 00:03:19,761
Askeladd, you said you weren't going
to stir up trouble for now.

18
00:03:19,841 --> 00:03:21,881
So that's Askeladd?

19
00:03:21,971 --> 00:03:24,681
I can't believe he objected
to the king's plan in front of him.

20
00:03:24,761 --> 00:03:27,311
Sorry, Your Highness.

21
00:03:29,521 --> 00:03:34,981
When it comes to Wales, I'm not going to back down.

22
00:03:36,941 --> 00:03:38,941
Explain your reasoning.

23
00:03:40,071 --> 00:03:41,611
Thank you.

24
00:03:43,361 --> 00:03:48,741
First, we've been fighting the English for 10 years.

25
00:03:49,951 --> 00:03:54,921
We should be focusing on recovery
for our people and our land right now.

26
00:03:55,001 --> 00:03:58,251
Another reason is that
the terrain in Wales is perilous,

27
00:03:58,341 --> 00:04:00,801
and as a result, the land is infertile.

28
00:04:01,921 --> 00:04:05,721
Attacking Wales would be like whipping our horses

29
00:04:05,801 --> 00:04:09,101
to make them jump off a cliff
just to catch a single rabbit.

30
00:04:10,101 --> 00:04:14,941
To put it simply, conquering Wales
isn't worth the cost.

31
00:04:16,731 --> 00:04:17,611
He's right.

32
00:04:17,691 --> 00:04:19,321
I'm glad he said it.

33
00:04:20,651 --> 00:04:22,491
He's good at talking.

34
00:04:23,491 --> 00:04:25,201
This isn't a conquest.

35
00:04:25,281 --> 00:04:28,411
The point is that we can't ignore those
who show disrespect for the king.

36
00:04:28,491 --> 00:04:29,791
Don't get the wrong idea.

37
00:04:29,871 --> 00:04:32,581
If that's what you're worried about,

38
00:04:33,911 --> 00:04:36,631
please, let me be your messenger.

39
00:04:36,711 --> 00:04:41,261
Allow me to show you that
I can persuade the people of Wales.

40
00:04:43,551 --> 00:04:48,261
Are you telling me, the king,
to show courtesy towards them?

41
00:04:48,351 --> 00:04:52,141
To the country you just called "a rabbit"?

42
00:04:52,221 --> 00:04:54,311
If you show courtesy,

43
00:04:54,391 --> 00:04:58,611
then they will understand your generosity.

44
00:04:58,691 --> 00:05:01,071
Please, listen to my entreaty.

45
00:05:13,041 --> 00:05:14,081
Is he going to kill him?

46
00:05:26,381 --> 00:05:29,141
This is how a loyal vassal should act.

47
00:05:30,351 --> 00:05:34,221
The greatest treasure anyone could ever
offer a king is words of advice.

48
00:05:34,311 --> 00:05:38,981
My army is filled with loyal
and brave men like this man.

49
00:05:39,691 --> 00:05:41,521
I am unworthy of your praise.

50
00:05:42,781 --> 00:05:44,321
How boring.

51
00:05:47,991 --> 00:05:50,621
Please, continue to lend me your aid.

52
00:05:57,661 --> 00:06:00,421
Wales or Canute, choose one.

53
00:06:02,461 --> 00:06:06,551
Honestly, I don't care about Wales.

54
00:06:07,631 --> 00:06:11,051
Give me Canute's head and join me,

55
00:06:11,141 --> 00:06:14,221
then I'll let Wales go free.

56
00:06:15,561 --> 00:06:18,481
I've looked into who you are a bit.

57
00:06:18,561 --> 00:06:21,401
Your mother really was a slave.

58
00:06:22,401 --> 00:06:25,731
I can guess why you're so caught up with Wales.

59
00:06:26,781 --> 00:06:29,491
The only merchandise that Wales produces

60
00:06:29,571 --> 00:06:32,411
is slaves.

61
00:06:38,211 --> 00:06:42,131
What do you think? It still sails.

62
00:06:42,211 --> 00:06:45,381
This is the ship you've always wanted to sail on.

63
00:06:45,461 --> 00:06:47,761
I can finally let you onboard.

64
00:06:54,301 --> 00:06:57,811
You can rest until Mord and the others return.

65
00:06:57,891 --> 00:07:00,271
-Hurry up. Bring it over here.
-Okay.

66
00:07:09,441 --> 00:07:11,361
-Is there still a lot left?
-Yes.

67
00:07:18,451 --> 00:07:20,331
What are you doing? Be careful!

68
00:07:41,691 --> 00:07:43,691
You must be hungry, right?

69
00:07:43,771 --> 00:07:47,231
Give me a minute. I have some good jerky.

70
00:07:48,691 --> 00:07:49,611
Thorfinn.

71
00:07:54,071 --> 00:07:56,781
Thorfinn? Where are you?

72
00:07:56,871 --> 00:07:58,791
Thorfinn?

73
00:08:05,041 --> 00:08:06,421
Thorfinn.

74
00:08:22,561 --> 00:08:24,521
I hate the way your face looks.

75
00:08:26,021 --> 00:08:32,741
I'm not going to let the crown rest
on top of a head like yours.

76
00:08:36,111 --> 00:08:37,701
Did he just say...?

77
00:08:38,911 --> 00:08:41,451
What did you just say?

78
00:08:43,501 --> 00:08:46,631
Are you deaf too, you old man?

79
00:08:46,711 --> 00:08:50,501
I said, how dare an ugly old man like you
wear something shiny?

80
00:08:53,051 --> 00:08:55,431
That's not what the face of a king looks like.

81
00:09:01,311 --> 00:09:02,721
Don't move, guards.

82
00:09:03,981 --> 00:09:06,941
The king is within reach of my sword.

83
00:09:11,401 --> 00:09:13,241
-Is he serious?
-Oh, dear.

84
00:09:18,201 --> 00:09:19,121
Askeladd.

85
00:09:20,581 --> 00:09:22,581
You bastard! King Sweyn is mine.

86
00:09:22,661 --> 00:09:24,001
Don't move, Thorkell!

87
00:09:24,081 --> 00:09:26,921
Askeladd's not acting normal. Don't provoke him.

88
00:09:32,631 --> 00:09:37,181
Put away your sword,
then I'll forgive you for this offense.

89
00:09:37,261 --> 00:09:38,841
Forgive me?

90
00:09:38,931 --> 00:09:41,641
Don't push your luck, you savage.

91
00:09:41,721 --> 00:09:44,851
As punishment for mocking my family and my people,

92
00:09:44,931 --> 00:09:47,231
you deserve to die!

93
00:09:47,311 --> 00:09:49,691
This is my last warning.

94
00:09:49,771 --> 00:09:53,691
Put away your sword, Askeladd.

95
00:09:53,781 --> 00:09:56,111
That's my nickname.

96
00:09:56,191 --> 00:10:00,031
I'll tell you the name my mother gave me.
My real name.

97
00:10:01,701 --> 00:10:05,411
Lucius Artorius Castus.

98
00:10:05,501 --> 00:10:11,591
I am the legitimate king who deserves
to rule over the land of Britannia.

99
00:10:15,211 --> 00:10:17,341
Now. Go!

100
00:10:45,541 --> 00:10:47,201
I feel better now.

101
00:10:55,631 --> 00:10:57,171
All right.

102
00:11:04,761 --> 00:11:07,221
What are you standing there for? Engage!

103
00:11:07,311 --> 00:11:09,021
Engage!

104
00:11:10,021 --> 00:11:12,811
This man is the criminal who murdered the king!

105
00:11:12,901 --> 00:11:14,361
Kill him!

106
00:11:18,691 --> 00:11:20,531
Hey, what's going on?

107
00:11:35,921 --> 00:11:36,881
What?

108
00:11:39,171 --> 00:11:41,381
What's he doing?

109
00:11:43,181 --> 00:11:45,051
What's going on?

110
00:11:46,301 --> 00:11:48,141
What's he doing?

111
00:11:48,221 --> 00:11:50,771
That idiot!

112
00:12:04,531 --> 00:12:05,661
What's wrong?

113
00:12:05,741 --> 00:12:08,291
Who wants to die next? Step up!

114
00:12:08,371 --> 00:12:12,911
The king of Britannia is going to kill you himself!

115
00:12:13,001 --> 00:12:16,421
Don't be afraid! Surround him!

116
00:12:22,631 --> 00:12:23,801
Die!

117
00:12:28,431 --> 00:12:29,641
Hurry up!

118
00:12:29,721 --> 00:12:31,931
-Don't push!
-You too!

119
00:12:32,021 --> 00:12:33,271
Out of my way!

120
00:12:33,351 --> 00:12:35,441
Damn. Out of my way!

121
00:12:36,651 --> 00:12:38,441
Askeladd!

122
00:12:44,151 --> 00:12:45,821
Hold it in, Thorkell.

123
00:12:45,911 --> 00:12:47,821
It's not your turn yet.

124
00:12:47,911 --> 00:12:50,371
I don't care anymore.

125
00:12:50,451 --> 00:12:52,161
He's gone mad.

126
00:12:52,251 --> 00:12:56,251
I hate it when someone steals my prey.

127
00:12:56,331 --> 00:12:59,251
He hasn't gone mad.

128
00:12:59,341 --> 00:13:00,711
He's putting on an act.

129
00:13:02,091 --> 00:13:07,091
He just chose to save both me and Wales.

130
00:13:07,181 --> 00:13:11,101
He's only feigning madness in order
to take the blame for killing the king.

131
00:13:12,311 --> 00:13:14,641
Let him run wild for a bit.

132
00:13:14,731 --> 00:13:16,311
I'll let you put it to an end.

133
00:13:20,021 --> 00:13:21,271
I don't care.

134
00:13:23,191 --> 00:13:24,401
Thorkell.

135
00:13:25,401 --> 00:13:28,451
I know he's your vassal,

136
00:13:28,531 --> 00:13:31,871
but a dog should be handled by his own master.

137
00:13:39,501 --> 00:13:42,131
What's wrong, Danes?

138
00:13:42,211 --> 00:13:44,131
Askeladd!

139
00:13:45,471 --> 00:13:47,551
You bastard.

140
00:13:47,631 --> 00:13:49,681
Do you have any idea what you've done?

141
00:13:49,761 --> 00:13:51,511
You killed the king.

142
00:13:51,601 --> 00:13:53,931
What are you talking about?

143
00:13:54,021 --> 00:13:56,141
I'm right here, alive and well.

144
00:13:57,351 --> 00:14:00,981
Shut up! You're the child of a slave!

145
00:14:02,611 --> 00:14:03,651
You swine.

146
00:14:04,821 --> 00:14:08,661
Is that how you talk to a king?

147
00:14:11,411 --> 00:14:13,201
Kneel down!

148
00:14:13,291 --> 00:14:16,791
I'll let you have the honor of kissing my shoes

149
00:14:16,871 --> 00:14:18,251
and then die!

150
00:14:20,751 --> 00:14:22,091
Askeladd!

151
00:14:24,921 --> 00:14:26,341
Stay back, Thorfinn!

152
00:14:54,621 --> 00:14:58,661
Is this the first time
you've stabbed someone, prince?

153
00:15:07,461 --> 00:15:08,761
You did well.

154
00:15:18,891 --> 00:15:20,691
Hey, Askeladd.

155
00:15:22,151 --> 00:15:23,981
Hey, that's...

156
00:15:24,061 --> 00:15:26,981
-Did he kill him?
-The prince! The prince did it!

157
00:15:37,371 --> 00:15:38,661
Stand straight.

158
00:15:39,661 --> 00:15:41,411
This part is important.

159
00:15:42,831 --> 00:15:45,381
This moment on stage was created for you.

160
00:15:45,461 --> 00:15:46,881
Don't waste it.

161
00:15:50,301 --> 00:15:54,141
Hey, baldie, what are you doing sleeping there?

162
00:15:54,221 --> 00:15:56,891
Damn. Damn.

163
00:15:56,971 --> 00:16:00,481
How could you let them stab you there, you idiot?

164
00:16:00,561 --> 00:16:02,061
Come on.

165
00:16:02,141 --> 00:16:03,771
Shut up.

166
00:16:05,191 --> 00:16:08,021
Let me rest.

167
00:16:08,111 --> 00:16:11,901
You bastard. Get up. We've got to run away.

168
00:16:13,201 --> 00:16:14,991
You fool.

169
00:16:15,071 --> 00:16:16,951
Just hurry up and do it.

170
00:16:17,951 --> 00:16:19,911
Sorry to make you wait.

171
00:16:21,251 --> 00:16:23,161
I'll give it to you.

172
00:16:23,251 --> 00:16:24,961
I'll give you my life.

173
00:16:26,921 --> 00:16:28,501
Kill me.

174
00:16:28,591 --> 00:16:32,171
We are-- We're enemies after all, right?

175
00:16:35,681 --> 00:16:36,971
Are you going to die?

176
00:16:38,641 --> 00:16:39,721
You?

177
00:16:40,721 --> 00:16:42,811
Hurry up.

178
00:16:43,811 --> 00:16:45,601
There's no time left.

179
00:16:50,651 --> 00:16:53,781
Are you trying to make a fool out of me? You bastard.

180
00:16:56,281 --> 00:16:58,241
It wasn't supposed to be like this!

181
00:16:58,321 --> 00:17:03,581
The duel to settle things between me and you
wasn't supposed to be like this!

182
00:17:03,661 --> 00:17:05,331
I won't forgive you.

183
00:17:05,421 --> 00:17:07,081
Don't die on me.

184
00:17:07,171 --> 00:17:10,591
Get up! Duel me right now!

185
00:17:10,671 --> 00:17:13,841
I'm the one who's supposed to defeat you!

186
00:17:13,921 --> 00:17:15,471
Hey, you!

187
00:17:15,551 --> 00:17:17,841
-You're kidding me! Hurry up and stand!
-Come on.

188
00:17:18,851 --> 00:17:21,101
This is why I hate kids.

189
00:17:21,181 --> 00:17:23,851
Duel me! Hey!

190
00:17:26,101 --> 00:17:27,311
How

191
00:17:28,311 --> 00:17:30,521
do you plan to live your life?

192
00:17:34,571 --> 00:17:36,991
In the future,

193
00:17:37,071 --> 00:17:39,451
after I die,

194
00:17:39,531 --> 00:17:43,041
how do you plan to live your life, Thorfinn?

195
00:17:47,371 --> 00:17:51,131
You haven't thought about it, right?

196
00:17:52,381 --> 00:17:53,961
Shut up.

197
00:17:54,051 --> 00:17:56,551
Move forward already.

198
00:17:56,631 --> 00:17:58,551
Don't stay

199
00:18:01,141 --> 00:18:04,391
stuck in a damn boring place like this forever.

200
00:18:05,851 --> 00:18:09,021
Go far ahead.

201
00:18:09,101 --> 00:18:12,821
Go beyond the world where Thors went.

202
00:18:12,901 --> 00:18:15,781
You're Thors' son. Go.

203
00:18:19,031 --> 00:18:21,031
That's

204
00:18:22,491 --> 00:18:24,491
your real fight.

205
00:18:27,541 --> 00:18:30,381
Become a true warrior,

206
00:18:31,631 --> 00:18:34,211
son of Thors.

207
00:19:04,281 --> 00:19:07,371
Thorfinn, I won't ask you to forgive me.

208
00:19:07,451 --> 00:19:11,001
He was dealt this punishment
because he went mad suddenly

209
00:19:11,081 --> 00:19:14,461
and committed the crime of murdering the king.

210
00:19:14,541 --> 00:19:19,761
However, I'm sure you don't feel like
serving me now that this has happened.

211
00:19:20,761 --> 00:19:22,511
Go wherever you want.

212
00:19:40,821 --> 00:19:41,701
Kill him!

213
00:19:41,781 --> 00:19:44,281
-He's a traitor!
-Stop!

214
00:19:44,371 --> 00:19:45,871
Don't kill him!

215
00:19:47,451 --> 00:19:50,501
Stand back. I will decide what to do with him.

216
00:19:52,001 --> 00:19:54,171
Thorkell, that's enough.

217
00:19:56,001 --> 00:19:59,131
Being stabbed is a small price to pay.

218
00:20:00,051 --> 00:20:03,891
Your Highness, you should have
your wounds treated in the inner chambers.

219
00:20:03,971 --> 00:20:06,931
Let me handle matters here.

220
00:20:07,011 --> 00:20:07,931
Take him.

221
00:20:09,851 --> 00:20:10,851
Floki.

222
00:20:12,391 --> 00:20:14,401
Now that the former king has passed,

223
00:20:14,481 --> 00:20:18,321
do you know who the commander
of the army in England is now?

224
00:20:19,481 --> 00:20:20,991
Well...

225
00:20:21,071 --> 00:20:22,571
What's wrong?

226
00:20:22,651 --> 00:20:23,821
Say it.

227
00:20:35,171 --> 00:20:37,291
Everyone, hear me.

228
00:20:38,421 --> 00:20:39,551
The former king,

229
00:20:39,631 --> 00:20:42,221
His Highness King Sweyn, has passed.

230
00:20:42,301 --> 00:20:44,971
From this day forth, I, Canute,

231
00:20:45,051 --> 00:20:48,511
shall act as the commander of the army
and the ruler of England!

232
00:20:52,181 --> 00:20:54,981
We will not pursue the subjugation of Wales.

233
00:20:55,061 --> 00:20:56,771
Now that the former king has passed,

234
00:20:56,851 --> 00:21:00,361
I predict that the remnants
of the English army will revolt.

235
00:21:00,441 --> 00:21:02,651
We must prepare to handle that first.

236
00:21:04,571 --> 00:21:07,991
I will provide further notice
regarding your rewards later.

237
00:21:09,031 --> 00:21:11,121
That is all. You are dismissed now.

238
00:21:19,841 --> 00:21:21,461
Hey.

239
00:21:41,151 --> 00:21:42,571
Hey.

240
00:21:42,651 --> 00:21:43,821
Hey, you.
